    "note": "APPROVE with zero MAJOR. The reviewer independently reproduced the 8/1/0 partition across the four dialects, ported both the IR recursive-descent parser and the three text expression parsers to a simulator with an inverse oracle, and ran 115 hand probes, 1,600 generated sources, about 158,000 fuzzed/mutation/random-byte inputs and cap boundary checks (256/257 rules, depth 64/65, 512/513 text bytes, source 65536, width 240/241, Work=0) with no fail-open, crash, hang, non-verbatim emission or quadratic blowup. Two MINORs were applied: (1) a quoted literal accepted C0 control bytes (NUL/ESC/VT) that the terminal renders as invisible cells, so parse_string now requires printable ASCII (0x20-0x7E) with three control regression pins; (2) the ABNF repetition is documented as the RFC 5234 prefix form '*(...)' only — a postfix '*' is an EBNF/PEG convention and stays fail-closed, matching the single ABNF fixture. The NITs (frontmatter-CRLF safe-direction fallback, the re-sliced header line, the nominal row-count off-by-one already re-gated downstream, and lenient-but-faithful parses such as empty IR args) are fail-closed or faithful with no corpus sample and match the approved siblings, so they are unchanged. The frontmatter key scanner trims before comparing, closing the cynefin-era 'config : 42' spacing bypass from the first draft."
